WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.075
There are two basic types of wireless networks: infrastructure, and ad hoc, otherwise known as point-to-point, or P2P.

00:08.075 --> 00:15.245
An infrastructure wireless network is one in which one or more wireless access points, like the one we see here, is the central point of the network.

00:15.245 --> 00:19.712
Clients connect to the network and possibly to each other through this wireless access point.

00:19.712 --> 00:28.129
And, the service set identifier, the SSID, of which we see one here, is the name for the network.

00:28.129 --> 00:38.241
The other type of wireless network, ad hoc, or P2P, has no central wireless access point. In this type of network, two devices wirelessly connect directly to each other.

00:38.241 --> 00:40.385
This is not very common for two reasons.

00:40.385 --> 00:51.542
First, an infrastructure network like this is easy to set up. Secondly, an ad hoc connection does not have the security nor encryption that an infrastructure network has.

